WEBVTT

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.900
So, what do you think of fall?

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:14.490
What?

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.370
I'm talking about the season. Do you like it?

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:19.930
I don't hate it, I suppose.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.760
What kind of music do you like, then?

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.500
Pop? J-Pop?

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.170
Or perhaps you're into classical music?

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:26.940
Senda!

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:27.910
What?

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.740
Keep your mouth shut when you're running.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.410
Who cares?

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:34.790
There's not much left here for us ninth-graders any—

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:38.800
So you're just going to give up on baseball after middle school?

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.230
As if!

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:43.290
You know very well that the real challenge starts next year.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.230
Can you write me a little note later?

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:48.100
Have it say, "Aim for the Koshien, Kei!
From Tsukishima Aoba," or something.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.040
Senda!

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.470
Can you just shut up?

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:53.490
Screw this.

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:56.600
I'm going to check out the high school team to prepare for next year instead.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:56.090
Here's the drink you wanted!

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:58.420
That was quick, Senda.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.990
Yep! I can run each base in four seconds flat, you know.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.620
But I have to say, you're pretty legit.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:09.100
You're already brown-nosing us for next year, eh?

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:12.330
I wouldn't say I'm <i>brown-nosing</i>...

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:17.990
How about you guys save the chit chat for later and start practicing instead?

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:21.080
Sorry, coach.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:23.880
I'm having a hard time tying the laces on my cleats.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.220
I see.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.640
Well then, give it your best.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:37.160
And I thought the school would fire his old ass for getting us eliminated in the 2nd round two summers in a row.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:39.180
He's quite a stubborn old fart.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:55.480
I Hate Him!

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.050
A sandlot baseball game?

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:03.900
Yeah.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:08.740
Some of the guys from the team you tricked into playing baseball

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:11.760
want to get back together to play a game.

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:15.810
We scraped together some guys we know to play against.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:18.460
And, of course, you'll be playing for us as well.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:20.140
That's fine.

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:22.990
It won't matter if we win or lose, as long as we have fun.

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:26.080
Nobody involved is on the team at school, either.

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:31.510
We're just a bunch of lazy guys who love to play but hate to practice.

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:35.050
There used to be that one stocky guy who was serious about it.

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:38.320
He gave up after three months.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:42.430
All right, let's put together another team.

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:44.230
We'll make brand-new uniforms, and—

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:45.630
Forget uniforms.

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:47.830
The game's this Sunday.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.200
Don't forget.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:50.590
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:56.270
Are these alarm clocks doing their job?

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:57.780
Yeah.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:05.290
One, two, three, four,

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:07.500
five, six, seven, eight.

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.660
One, two, three, four,

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:12.140
five, six, seven, eight.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:15.140
I brought in all the seventh- and eighth-graders, Captain.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:18.040
The ninth-graders are all here, too, except for Senda.

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:20.680
Forget him.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:23.670
He's probably busy catering himself to the high school team.

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:25.250
Captain...

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:26.100
Yeah?

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:30.510
Have you heard the rumors about the high school team?

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:34.010
Yeah, I've heard the rumors.

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:48.300
Are they just rumors?

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:49.630
Who knows.

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:52.180
I guess I'll find out next year.

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:55.730
By the way, how's Kitamura doing these days?

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:59.000
How am <i>I</i> supposed to know how he's doing?

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:01.660
Has he not been showing up at the batting center?

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:02.610
Like I said...

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:04.510
...I don't know anything!

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:11.680
Then would you care to explain why the leotard disappeared after <i>you</i> passed by the girl's gymnastics club room?

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:14.890
I wasn't the only one who passed by that room, you know.

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:19.480
Aside from Kitamura, there was just this one guy dressed all in black and wearing a ski mask.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:20.980
It's him!

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:21.960
It's got to be him!

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:23.670
Mr. Akichi!

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:26.070
A man wearing a ski mask, dressed all in black

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:28.200
just turned himself in holding the leotard.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:29.480
What?

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:32.640
So you mean to say that the man with the ski mask, dressed all in black did it?

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:34.210
Bravo, Sherlock.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:36.730
I'll be on my way now.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:38.260
Kitamura.

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:42.510
You're quick on your feet and you have decent P.E. grades.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:46.910
You should make use of your talents and join a sports team in high school.

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:49.040
You don't want to end up stealing leotards, now do you?

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:50.310
Gimme a break, old man.

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:07.140
The fall sports season, huh?

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:27.550
How nice of you to come by, Ko.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:28.590
You here for some coffee?

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:30.830
Nope, I wanted to swing by the cages.

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:31.810
Who's inside?

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.610
He hasn't been around here for quite some time.

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:37.630
But it sounds like he still bats quite regularly.

00:07:37.630 --> 00:07:39.040
Okay, but who is it?

00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:58.290
Ain'tcha gonna go slug some?

00:07:58.290 --> 00:07:59.990
Here's one on the house.

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:04.330
Nah, I'm going to head home.

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:05.650
Ko...

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:14.150
Winning or losing doesn't matter as long as you have fun, huh?

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:45.070
Time for laundry!

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:48.010
Come on, Aoba.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:52.360
You should act more like a lady now that you're in eighth grade.

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:54.050
Whatever you say.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:57.550
Where's Dad?

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:59.080
He's at the town meeting.

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:03.570
Just when I was about to have him play catch with me...

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:06.930
Don't you do that enough every day during baseball practice?

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:11.730
You want me to play with you instead?

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:13.540
You?

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:29.930
That was good!

00:09:29.930 --> 00:09:31.540
You really <i>are</i> my little sister.

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:35.820
Well, I've been playing a lot of catch with Ko.

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:38.260
With Ko?

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:56.750
All right.

00:09:58.390 --> 00:10:00.040
Is Ko going to pitch for you guys?

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:01.300
Yeah.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:04.040
You won't have to worry about getting hit, at least.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.080
He's got control, I guarantee it.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:07.820
We'll have to see about that.

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:10.280
There's no bigger kill-joy than being walked all day, you know.

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:13.020
I'll hit everything straight out of the park!

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:15.170
Yeah, let's have some fun.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:17.830
That's the best way to play baseball.

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:20.970
Let's throw some warmup balls, Nakanishi!

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:21.800
Sure.

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:30.240
How long has it been since we last paired up as a battery?

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:33.650
It was back in sixth grade, so I guess three years ago.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:34.860
Oh yeah.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:39.750
Let's take it easy and start light for now.

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:40.970
Sure thing.

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:02.270
Change pitchers.

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:06.790
Oh, come on now, Nakanishi.

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:09.020
We haven't even started playing yet.

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:10.280
You take right field.

00:11:10.280 --> 00:11:12.760
I said, hang on!

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:15.020
I'll throw hard once we actually start playing, okay?

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:16.330
"Hard"?

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:18.150
You're the one who said,

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:20.710
"Take it easy and start light for now."

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:21.660
That's why...

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:23.210
That was "light"?

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:25.730
Tanaka, you're pitching.

00:11:25.730 --> 00:11:27.670
Are you even listening?

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:36.310
We can stop if your hands are hurting, Momiji.

00:11:36.310 --> 00:11:38.040
I'm fine.

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:41.410
Ko and I would play catch for more than half a day some of the times.

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:45.980
<i>Don't think of Ko as just another boy!</i>

00:11:47.090 --> 00:11:48.070
Ao!

00:11:48.070 --> 00:11:49.720
Oh, right.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:55.890
<i>Once he gets serious, he could become the best pitcher in Japan!</i>

00:11:56.120 --> 00:11:58.730
<i>He might even be able to throw 160 km/h.</i>

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:01.500
As if!

00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:03.860
Sorry, Momiji!

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:05.390
No worries.

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:06.640
I'm used to it.

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:11.980
Thanks for playing with me.

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:13.780
I think that's enough.

00:12:45.940 --> 00:12:47.010
One out!

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:51.720
Right field!

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:53.150
I got it!

00:12:53.150 --> 00:12:54.850
You ain't got shit!

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:56.750
I'm headed for an infield home run!

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:00.760
Run back!

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:03.940
Double play!

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:04.700
Change sides!

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:17.430
That was awesome!

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:19.540
He made that infield homer look easy!

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:20.590
Did you see that?

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:49.810
<i>Why don't you join the team instead of just staring at them like that?</i>

00:13:56.720 --> 00:14:01.690
Why don't you guys join the team instead of just staring at them like that?

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:04.930
Who'd want to join a crappy team like that?

00:14:04.930 --> 00:14:07.730
We're levels apart.

00:14:07.730 --> 00:14:10.060
That might be true now,

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:14.470
but they'll get ahead of you guys if you just sit around doing nothing.

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:15.820
What did you say?

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:17.960
Who the hell do you think you're talking—

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:21.830
Tsukishima didn't say anything wrong, now did she?

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:24.350
No, not at all.

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:26.270
Sorry, Tsukishima.

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:29.610
We just don't really feel up to playing baseball right now.

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:30.870
I see.

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:33.630
Sorry for bothering you guys then.

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:35.080
Tsukishima.

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:35.720
Yes?

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:38.290
There's nothing to apologize for.

00:14:56.630 --> 00:14:57.980
Change sides!

00:14:59.990 --> 00:15:02.180
I see you got some familiar faces together, there.

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:07.550
Didn't you let Kitamura pitch back in grade school?

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:08.500
Yeah.

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:11.190
Aren't you going to let him pitch today?

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:15.660
I wanted to have a <i>fun</i> sandlot game today.

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:21.220
It's the last inning, and we're down by a run.

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:24.540
There are two outs, but we've got runners on first and second.

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:27.370
We'll tie the score with a single
or make a comeback if I hit a long one.

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:32.540
Here's the single!

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:34.950
All right, we'll tie it up first!

00:15:44.690 --> 00:15:46.140
O-Out!

00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:47.430
That's the game!

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:52.210
I see.

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:55.070
A "fun" game, huh?

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:02.550
Hey, good game, man.

00:16:02.550 --> 00:16:05.180
It was good to finally play a sandlot game again.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:09.650
What are you thinking?

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:13.700
Nakanishi, Kitamura.

00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:16.260
See you guys around.

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:40.310
Throw it hard this time.

00:16:40.550 --> 00:16:41.760
Hard?

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:42.900
Yeah.

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:45.310
Don't take it easy and throw it light.

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:47.080
Pitch one with all you've got.

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:48.840
All right!

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:52.160
I said pitch, not waste time.

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:15.960
Sorry.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:17.420
I guess that was too hard.

00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:22.280
Why?

00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:22.820
Huh?

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:27.470
Why didn't you join the baseball team when you can pitch like this?

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:29.800
Ow...

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:31.620
Uh, reality check?

00:17:32.270 --> 00:17:34.030
You're the reason why I didn't join, remember?

00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:36.370
I-I was?

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:45.310
I heard this rumor...

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:47.910
Rumors again?

00:17:48.190 --> 00:17:50.910
Is it true that when you guys joined the baseball team,

00:17:51.650 --> 00:17:53.780
the ninth-graders were a bunch of delinquents?

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:56.470
"Delinquents" doesn't begin to describe it.

00:17:58.610 --> 00:17:59.560
They're scumbags.

00:18:00.710 --> 00:18:06.730
I would have quit the team within three months if it wasn't for Nakanishi.

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:18.870
I went over to the baseball team club room that day with my application form.

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:20.680
And then...

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:49.220
But that was three months after school started!

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:51.140
What were you doing <i>before</i> then?

00:18:51.430 --> 00:18:54.900
I thought I asked you to join me at the beginning of the school year?

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:57.470
I didn't have the confidence.

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:05.160
But as I kept practicing at home and scoping out the baseball practices at school,

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:07.250
I thought maybe I could actually do it.

00:19:07.990 --> 00:19:10.690
And then, <i>that</i> happened.

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:13.360
Fine, okay.

00:19:13.810 --> 00:19:15.060
But who cares.

00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:18.090
Thanks to that, we got to have some fun playing sandlot baseball.

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:20.360
Let's make another team and play again.

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:23.010
Of course, this time, with brand-new uniforms—

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:24.480
Screw uniforms.

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:26.120
I see.

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:35.750
So those scumbags will be there waiting

00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:40.160
when you join the high school team next year, huh?

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:42.260
Yeah, I'm looking forward to it.

00:19:43.770 --> 00:19:45.800
Do you think you'll get along with them?

00:19:45.800 --> 00:19:50.730
You'd be hard-pressed to find <i>anyone</i> who could get along with guys like that.

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:54.450
You've got mud on your cleats, Makihara.

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:55.910
Oh, thanks, Senda.

00:19:58.180 --> 00:20:01.480
But do you think things will be okay next year?

00:20:01.480 --> 00:20:03.410
It looks like we won't be getting a new coach.

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:04.460
You dumbass.

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:05.780
It won't be like this year.

00:20:06.070 --> 00:20:08.040
This year sucked because they got a crappy coach

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:11.200
who wanted to make a team out of a bunch of crappy twelfth-graders.

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:15.990
We would have gotten to the quarterfinals if he had used us eleventh-graders properly.

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:21.630
So naturally, the team's going to be strong when we become the twelfth-graders.

00:20:22.010 --> 00:20:23.200
We might make the top four—

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:27.910
If we get lucky, we could even make the finals!

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:32.740
The school seems to want us to go all the way to Koshien.

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:36.110
To spectate, you mean?

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.550
Perhaps.

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:48.250
This is excellent, Daimon.

00:20:48.250 --> 00:20:50.140
Thank you, Principal.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:52.460
Don't get ahead of yourself now.

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:55.300
I'm only the Acting Principal, as you can see.

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:57.740
Acting Principal.

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:00.330
My apologies.

00:21:23.460 --> 00:21:24.960
Coming home from practice?

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:26.350
That's none of your business.

00:21:26.810 --> 00:21:29.380
I guess it isn't.

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:14.870
<i>I'm not lying about his talent, Akaishi!</i>

00:23:14.870 --> 00:23:15.510
<i>Too late.</i>

00:23:15.510 --> 00:23:16.590
<i>No it's not!</i>

00:23:16.590 --> 00:23:19.680
<i>I'm saying, you recognized his skills way too late.</i>

00:23:20.110 --> 00:23:20.890
<i>Who's that?</i>

00:23:20.890 --> 00:23:21.720
<i>Hell if I know.</i>

00:23:22.140 --> 00:23:23.670
<i>I don't mind this,</i>

00:23:23.670 --> 00:23:26.470
<i>but why do we have to practice in secret like this?</i>

00:23:26.470 --> 00:23:28.720
<i>You're our secret weapon, that's why.</i>

00:23:29.140 --> 00:23:31.390
<i>Next time, on Cross Game Episode Four:</i>

00:23:31.390 --> 00:23:32.420
<i>Secret Weapon.</i>

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:34.630
<i>Did Aoba tell you something?</i>

00:23:34.960 --> 00:23:37.780
<i>No, Wakaba did.</i>
